IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `snap-core`
IMPORT `snap1-logic`

-- 7 U.S.C. 2014(d): what household income includes, and the nineteen exclusions.
-- SOURCE: usc07-ch51.txt (a converter's rendering, not the official text).
-- Shape: one function per paragraph, taking only the facts that paragraph reads; each answers JUST TRUE when the paragraph excludes the
-- item, JUST FALSE where the paragraph itself says the item is NOT excluded, and NOTHING otherwise ("this paragraph does not reach it").
-- `s 2014(d) the item is included in household income` then reads the closed list: "excluding only" makes an item that no paragraph excludes JUST FALSE on exclusion.
-- Money is a NUMBER of dollars. A paragraph that excludes only part of an item answers with the DOLLARS excluded.

§ `s 2014(d) Exclusions from income`

-- src:224 | Household income for purposes of the supplemental nutrition assistance program shall include all income from whatever source excluding only—
@ref s 2014(d), the chapeau (src:224)
GIVEN `the answers of the paragraphs of subsection (d) for the item` IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(d) the item is included in household income` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF any `snap1 is definitely yes` `the answers of the paragraphs of subsection (d) for the item`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall include all income from whatever source excluding only" the listed paragraphs, so an item one of them excludes is not included
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "shall include all income from whatever source"

-- src:225 | any gain or benefit which is not in the form of money payable directly to a household (notwithstanding its conversion in whole or in part to direct payments to households pursuant to any demonstration project carried out or authorized under Federal law including demonstration projects created by the waiver of provisions of Federal law);
@ref s 2014(d)(1) (src:225)
GIVEN `the item is a gain or benefit that is not in the form of money payable directly to a household (even if converted to direct payments under a demonstration project)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(d)(1) the item is excluded because it is not money payable directly to a household` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the item is a gain or benefit that is not in the form of money payable directly to a household (even if converted to direct payments under a demonstration project)`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "excluding only— (1) any gain or benefit which is not in the form of money payable directly to a household"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (1) reaches only a gain or benefit that is not money payable directly to a household

-- src:226 | any income in the certification period which is received too infrequently or irregularly to be reasonably anticipated, but not in excess of $30 in a quarter, subject to modification by the Secretary in light of subsection (f);
@ref s 2014(d)(2) (src:226)
GIVEN `the income is received in the certification period too infrequently or irregularly to be reasonably anticipated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of it received in the quarter, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the quarterly limit as modified by the Secretary in light of subsection (f), if the Secretary has modified it` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2014(d)(2) the amount excluded in the quarter` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the income is received in the certification period too infrequently or irregularly to be reasonably anticipated`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (2) reaches only income "received too infrequently or irregularly to be reasonably anticipated"
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `the quarterly limit as modified by the Secretary in light of subsection (f), if the Secretary has modified it`
                WHEN JUST limit THEN JUST (minimum (LIST `the amount of it received in the quarter, in dollars`, limit))
                WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST (minimum (LIST `the amount of it received in the quarter, in dollars`, 30))

-- src:227 | (3) all educational loans on which payment is deferred, grants, scholarships, fellowships, veterans’ educational benefits, and the like—
-- src:228 | (A) awarded to a household member enrolled at a recognized institution of post-secondary education, at a school for the handicapped, in a vocational education program, or in a program that provides for completion of a secondary school diploma or obtaining the equivalent thereof;
-- src:229 | (B) to the extent that they do not exceed the amount used for or made available as an allowance determined by such school, institution, program, or other grantor, for tuition and mandatory fees (including the rental or purchase of any equipment, materials, and supplies related to the pursuit of the course of study involved), books, supplies, transportation, and other miscellaneous personal expenses (other than living expenses), of the student incidental to attending such school, institution, or program; and
-- src:230 | (C) to the extent loans include any origination fees and insurance premiums;
@ref s 2014(d)(3) (src:227-230)
GIVEN `the item is an educational loan on which payment is deferred, a grant, a scholarship, a fellowship, a veterans' educational benefit, or the like` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is awarded to a household member enrolled at a recognized institution of post-secondary education, at a school for the handicapped, in a vocational education program, or in a program that provides for completion of a secondary school diploma or its equivalent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the monthly amount of the item, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the allowance determined by the school, institution, program or grantor for tuition and mandatory fees, books, supplies, transportation and other miscellaneous personal expenses (other than living expenses), in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the origination fees and insurance premiums that the loan includes, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2014(d)(3) the amount excluded` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF  (NOT `the item is an educational loan on which payment is deferred, a grant, a scholarship, a fellowship, a veterans' educational benefit, or the like`)
            OR (NOT `it is awarded to a household member enrolled at a recognized institution of post-secondary education, at a school for the handicapped, in a vocational education program, or in a program that provides for completion of a secondary school diploma or its equivalent`)
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (3) reaches only such awards to an enrolled household member
        OTHERWISE
            JUST (minimum (LIST `the monthly amount of the item, in dollars`, `the allowance determined by the school, institution, program or grantor for tuition and mandatory fees, books, supplies, transportation and other miscellaneous personal expenses (other than living expenses), in dollars` PLUS `the origination fees and insurance premiums that the loan includes, in dollars`))

-- src:231 | (4) all loans other than educational loans on which repayment is deferred;
@ref s 2014(d)(4) (src:231)
GIVEN `the item is a loan, other than an educational loan, on which repayment is deferred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(d)(4) the loan is excluded` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the item is a loan, other than an educational loan, on which repayment is deferred`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "all loans other than educational loans on which repayment is deferred"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (4) reaches only loans on which repayment is deferred

-- src:232 | reimbursements which do not exceed expenses actually incurred and which do not represent a gain or benefit to the household and any allowance a State agency provides no more frequently than annually to families with children on the occasion of those children’s entering or returning to school or child care for the purpose of obtaining school clothes (except that no such allowance shall be excluded if the State agency reduces monthly assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.) in the month for which the allowance is provided): Provided, That no portion of benefits provided under title IV–A of the Social Security Act [42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.], to the extent it is attributable to an adjustment for work-related or child care expenses (except for payments or reimbursements for such expenses made under an employment, education, or training program initiated under such title after September 19, 1988), and no portion of any educational loan on which payment is deferred, grant, scholarship, fellowship, veterans’ benefits, and the like that are provided for living expenses, shall be considered such reimbursement;
@ref s 2014(d)(5) (src:232)
GIVEN `the item is a reimbursement that does not exceed expenses actually incurred and does not represent a gain or benefit to the household` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the item is an allowance a State agency provides no more frequently than annually to a family with children on the occasion of the children's entering or returning to school or child care, for school clothes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency reduces monthly assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV in the month for which the allowance is provided` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the item is a portion of title IV-A benefits attributable to an adjustment for work-related or child care expenses, other than a payment made under an employment, education or training program initiated under that title after September 19, 1988` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the item is a portion of an educational loan on which payment is deferred, a grant, a scholarship, a fellowship, a veterans' benefit or the like that is provided for living expenses` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(d)(5) the item is excluded as a reimbursement or a school allowance` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the item is a portion of title IV-A benefits attributable to an adjustment for work-related or child care expenses, other than a payment made under an employment, education or training program initiated under that title after September 19, 1988`
            OR `the item is a portion of an educational loan on which payment is deferred, a grant, a scholarship, a fellowship, a veterans' benefit or the like that is provided for living expenses`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no portion of benefits provided under title IV–A of the Social Security Act ... shall be considered such reimbursement"
        IF `the item is an allowance a State agency provides no more frequently than annually to a family with children on the occasion of the children's entering or returning to school or child care, for school clothes`
            AND `the State agency reduces monthly assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV in the month for which the allowance is provided`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no such allowance shall be excluded if the State agency reduces monthly assistance"
        IF `the item is a reimbursement that does not exceed expenses actually incurred and does not represent a gain or benefit to the household`
            OR `the item is an allowance a State agency provides no more frequently than annually to a family with children on the occasion of the children's entering or returning to school or child care, for school clothes`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "reimbursements which do not exceed expenses actually incurred ... and any allowance a State agency provides no more frequently than annually"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (5) reaches only the reimbursements and the school allowance it describes

-- src:233 | moneys received and used for the care and maintenance of a third-party beneficiary who is not a household member, and child support payments made by a household member to or for an individual who is not a member of the household if the household member is legally obligated to make the payments;
@ref s 2014(d)(6) (src:233)
GIVEN `the item is money received and used for the care and maintenance of a third-party beneficiary who is not a household member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the item is a child support payment made by a household member to or for an individual who is not a member of the household` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the household member is legally obligated to make the payments` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(d)(6) the item is excluded as care and maintenance of a third party or child support paid out` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the item is money received and used for the care and maintenance of a third-party beneficiary who is not a household member`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "moneys received and used for the care and maintenance of a third-party beneficiary who is not a household member"
        IF `the item is a child support payment made by a household member to or for an individual who is not a member of the household` AND `the household member is legally obligated to make the payments`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "child support payments made by a household member to or for an individual who is not a member of the household if the household member is legally obligated to make the payments"
        IF `the item is a child support payment made by a household member to or for an individual who is not a member of the household`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "child support payments made by a household member to or for an individual who is not a member of the household if the household member is legally obligated to make the payments" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a))
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (6) reaches only those two kinds of item

-- src:234 | (7) income earned by a child who is a member of the household, who is an elementary or secondary school student, and who is 17 years of age or younger;
@ref s 2014(d)(7) (src:234)
GIVEN `the income is earned by a child who is a member of the household` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child is an elementary or secondary school student` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child's age in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(d)(7) the child's earned income is excluded` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the income is earned by a child who is a member of the household` AND `the child is an elementary or secondary school student` AND `the child's age in years` AT MOST 17
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "income earned by a child who is a member of the household, who is an elementary or secondary school student, and who is 17 years of age or younger"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (7) reaches only a child member who is a school student aged 17 or younger

-- src:235 | moneys received in the form of nonrecurring lump-sum payments, including, but not limited to, income tax refunds, rebates, or credits, cash donations based on need that are received from one or more private nonprofit charitable organizations, but not in excess of $300 in the aggregate in a quarter, retroactive lump-sum social security or railroad retirement pension payments and retroactive lump-sum insurance settlements: Provided, That such payments shall be counted as resources, unless specifically excluded by other laws;
@ref s 2014(d)(8) (src:235)
GIVEN `the item is a cash donation based on need received from one or more private nonprofit charitable organizations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the donations received in the quarter, in the aggregate, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2014(d)(8) the cash donation excluded in the quarter` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the item is a cash donation based on need received from one or more private nonprofit charitable organizations`
            THEN JUST (minimum (LIST `the amount of the donations received in the quarter, in the aggregate, in dollars`, 300))
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the $300 limit is on "cash donations based on need that are received from one or more private nonprofit charitable organizations"

-- src:235 | moneys received in the form of nonrecurring lump-sum payments, including, but not limited to, income tax refunds, rebates, or credits, cash donations based on need that are received from one or more private nonprofit charitable organizations, but not in excess of $300 in the aggregate in a quarter, retroactive lump-sum social security or railroad retirement pension payments and retroactive lump-sum insurance settlements: Provided, That such payments shall be counted as resources, unless specifically excluded by other laws;
@ref s 2014(d)(8) (src:235)
GIVEN `the item is a nonrecurring lump-sum payment (an income tax refund, rebate or credit, a retroactive lump-sum social security or railroad retirement pension payment, a retroactive lump-sum insurance settlement, or another nonrecurring lump sum)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(d)(8) the lump-sum payment is excluded from income` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the item is a nonrecurring lump-sum payment (an income tax refund, rebate or credit, a retroactive lump-sum social security or railroad retirement pension payment, a retroactive lump-sum insurance settlement, or another nonrecurring lump sum)`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "moneys received in the form of nonrecurring lump-sum payments, including, but not limited to, income tax refunds"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (8) reaches nonrecurring lump-sum payments; the cash donations of the same paragraph are measured by the quarterly limit

-- src:235 | (8) moneys received in the form of nonrecurring lump-sum payments, including, but not limited to, income tax refunds, rebates, or credits, cash donations based on need that are received from one or more private nonprofit charitable organizations, but not in excess of $300 in the aggregate in a quarter, retroactive lump-sum social security or railroad retirement pension payments and retroactive lump-sum insurance settlements: Provided, That such payments shall be counted as resources, unless specifically excluded by other laws;
@ref s 2014(d)(8), the proviso (src:235)
GIVEN `another law specifically excludes the payment from resources` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(d)(8) the excluded payment is counted as a resource` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `another law specifically excludes the payment from resources`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "such payments shall be counted as resources, unless specifically excluded by other laws"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "such payments shall be counted as resources"

-- src:236 | (9) the cost of producing self-employed income, but household income that otherwise is included under this subsection shall be reduced by the extent that the cost of producing self-employment income exceeds the income derived from self-employment as a farmer;
@ref s 2014(d)(9) (src:236)
GIVEN `the cost of producing self-employment income, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2014(d)(9) the cost of producing self-employed income that is excluded` MEANS `the cost of producing self-employment income, in dollars`

-- src:236 | (9) the cost of producing self-employed income, but household income that otherwise is included under this subsection shall be reduced by the extent that the cost of producing self-employment income exceeds the income derived from self-employment as a farmer;
@ref s 2014(d)(9) (src:236)
GIVEN `the cost of producing self-employment income, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the income derived from self-employment as a farmer, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2014(d)(9) the reduction of the other income that is included` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the cost of producing self-employment income, in dollars` GREATER THAN `the income derived from self-employment as a farmer, in dollars`
            THEN `the cost of producing self-employment income, in dollars` MINUS `the income derived from self-employment as a farmer, in dollars`
        OTHERWISE 0

-- src:237 | (10) any income that any other Federal law specifically excludes from consideration as income for purposes of determining eligibility for the supplemental nutrition assistance program except as otherwise provided in subsection (k) of this section;
@ref s 2014(d)(10) (src:237)
GIVEN `another Federal law specifically excludes the income from consideration as income for purposes of determining eligibility for the program` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (k) otherwise provides for the income` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(d)(10) the income is excluded because another Federal law excludes it` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `another Federal law specifically excludes the income from consideration as income for purposes of determining eligibility for the program` AND `subsection (k) otherwise provides for the income`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except as otherwise provided in subsection (k) of this section"
        IF `another Federal law specifically excludes the income from consideration as income for purposes of determining eligibility for the program`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "any income that any other Federal law specifically excludes from consideration as income"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (10) reaches only income another Federal law "specifically excludes"

-- src:238 | (11)
-- src:239 | (A) any payments or allowances made for the purpose of providing energy assistance under any Federal law (other than part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.)); or
-- src:240 | (B) a 1-time payment or allowance made under a Federal or State law for the costs of weatherization or emergency repair or replacement of an unsafe or inoperative furnace or other heating or cooling device;
@ref s 2014(d)(11) (src:238-240)
GIVEN `the payment or allowance is made for the purpose of providing energy assistance under a Federal law other than part A of title IV of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment or allowance is a 1-time payment made under a Federal or State law for the costs of weatherization or emergency repair or replacement of an unsafe or inoperative furnace or other heating or cooling device` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(d)(11) the payment or allowance is excluded` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the payment or allowance is made for the purpose of providing energy assistance under a Federal law other than part A of title IV of the Social Security Act`
            OR `the payment or allowance is a 1-time payment made under a Federal or State law for the costs of weatherization or emergency repair or replacement of an unsafe or inoperative furnace or other heating or cooling device`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: paragraph (11)(A) or (B)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (11) reaches energy assistance under a Federal law other than part A of title IV, and a 1-time weatherization or repair payment

-- src:241 | through September 30 of any fiscal year, any increase in income attributable to a cost-of-living adjustment made on or after July 1 of such fiscal year under title II or XVI of the Social Security Act [42 U.S.C. 401 et seq., 1381 et seq.], section 3(a)(1) of the Railroad Retirement Act of 1974 (45 U.S.C. 231b(a)(1)), or section 5312 of title 38, if the household was certified as eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program or received an allotment in the month immediately preceding the first month in which the adjustment was effective;
@ref s 2014(d)(12) (src:241)
GIVEN `the date the cost-of-living adjustment was made` IS A DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
      `the increase is attributable to a cost-of-living adjustment under title II or XVI of the Social Security Act, section 3(a)(1) of the Railroad Retirement Act of 1974, or section 5312 of title 38` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the household was certified as eligible or received an allotment in the month immediately preceding the first month in which the adjustment was effective` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(d)(12) the cost-of-living increase is excluded on the date` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the increase is attributable to a cost-of-living adjustment under title II or XVI of the Social Security Act, section 3(a)(1) of the Railroad Retirement Act of 1974, or section 5312 of title 38`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (12) reaches "any increase in income attributable to a cost-of-living adjustment" under those provisions
        IF NOT `the household was certified as eligible or received an allotment in the month immediately preceding the first month in which the adjustment was effective`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the household was certified as eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program or received an allotment in the month immediately preceding the first month in which the adjustment was effective" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a))
        IF  DATE_MONTH `the date the cost-of-living adjustment was made` AT LEAST 7
            AND DATE_MONTH `the date the cost-of-living adjustment was made` AT MOST 9
            AND `the date asked about` AT MOST Date 30 9 (DATE_YEAR `the date the cost-of-living adjustment was made`)
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "through September 30 of any fiscal year, any increase in income attributable to a cost-of-living adjustment made on or after July 1 of such fiscal year"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (12) runs "through September 30" of the fiscal year of an adjustment made on or after July 1

-- src:242 | (13) any payment made to the household under section 3507 [Footnote: 1 See References in Text note below.] of title 26 (relating to advance payment of earned income credit);
@ref s 2014(d)(13) (src:242)
GIVEN `the payment is made to the household under section 3507 of title 26 (advance payment of earned income credit)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(d)(13) the advance earned income credit payment is excluded` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the payment is made to the household under section 3507 of title 26 (advance payment of earned income credit)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (13) reaches only payments under section 3507 of title 26

-- src:243 | (14) any payment made to the household under section 2015(d)(4)(I) of this title or a pilot project under section 2025(h)(1)(F) of this title for work related expenses or for dependent care;
@ref s 2014(d)(14) (src:243)
GIVEN `the payment is made to the household under section 2015(d)(4)(I) or a pilot project under section 2025(h)(1)(F)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is for work related expenses or for dependent care` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(d)(14) the payment for work related expenses or dependent care is excluded` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the payment is made to the household under section 2015(d)(4)(I) or a pilot project under section 2025(h)(1)(F)` AND `it is for work related expenses or for dependent care` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (14) reaches only such payments for work related expenses or dependent care

-- src:244 | (15) any amounts necessary for the fulfillment of a plan for achieving self-support of a household member as provided under subparagraph (A)(iii) or (B)(iv) of section 1612(b)(4) of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 1382a(b)(4));
@ref s 2014(d)(15) (src:244)
GIVEN `the amount is necessary for the fulfillment of a plan for achieving self-support of a household member under subparagraph (A)(iii) or (B)(iv) of section 1612(b)(4) of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(d)(15) the amount for a plan for achieving self-support is excluded` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the amount is necessary for the fulfillment of a plan for achieving self-support of a household member under subparagraph (A)(iii) or (B)(iv) of section 1612(b)(4) of the Social Security Act` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (15) reaches only amounts necessary for such a plan

-- src:245 | at the option of the State agency, any educational loans on which payment is deferred, grants, scholarships, fellowships, veterans’ educational benefits, and the like (other than loans, grants, scholarships, fellowships, veterans’ educational benefits, and the like excluded under paragraph (3)), to the extent that they are required to be excluded under title XIX of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 1396 et seq.);
@ref s 2014(d)(16) (src:245)
GIVEN `the State agency has chosen to exclude such educational awards` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the item is an educational loan on which payment is deferred, a grant, a scholarship, a fellowship, a veterans' educational benefit, or the like, not excluded under paragraph (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is required to be excluded under title XIX of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(d)(16) the educational award is excluded at the option of the State agency` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency has chosen to exclude such educational awards` AND `the item is an educational loan on which payment is deferred, a grant, a scholarship, a fellowship, a veterans' educational benefit, or the like, not excluded under paragraph (3)` AND `it is required to be excluded under title XIX of the Social Security Act`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "at the option of the State agency, any educational loans ... to the extent that they are required to be excluded under title XIX"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (16) reaches only what the State agency has chosen to exclude and title XIX requires to be excluded

-- src:246 | (17) at the option of the State agency, any State complementary assistance program payments that are excluded for the purpose of determining eligibility for medical assistance under section 1931 of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 1396u–1);
@ref s 2014(d)(17) (src:246)
GIVEN `the State agency has chosen to exclude State complementary assistance payments` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payments are excluded for the purpose of determining eligibility for medical assistance under section 1931 of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(d)(17) the State complementary assistance payment is excluded at the option of the State agency` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency has chosen to exclude State complementary assistance payments` AND `the payments are excluded for the purpose of determining eligibility for medical assistance under section 1931 of the Social Security Act`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "at the option of the State agency, any State complementary assistance program payments that are excluded"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (17) reaches only what the State agency has chosen to exclude and section 1931 excludes

-- src:247 | at the option of the State agency, any types of income that the State agency does not consider when determining eligibility for (A) cash assistance under a program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.) or the amount of such assistance, or (B) medical assistance under section 1931 of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 1396u–1), except that this paragraph does not authorize a State agency to exclude wages or salaries, benefits under title I, II, IV, X, XIV, or XVI of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 301 et seq. [, 401 et seq., 601 et seq., 1201 et seq., 1351 et seq., 1381 et seq.]), regular payments from a government source (such as unemployment benefits and general assistance), worker’s compensation, child support payments made to a household member by an individual who is legally obligated to make the payments, or such other types of income the consideration of which the Secretary determines by regulation to be essential to equitable determinations of eligibility and benefit levels; and
@ref s 2014(d)(18) (src:247)
GIVEN `the State agency has chosen to exclude such types of income` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency does not consider the income when determining eligibility for cash assistance under part A of title IV, the amount of such assistance, or medical assistance under section 1931` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the income is wages or salaries, benefits under title I, II, IV, X, XIV, or XVI of the Social Security Act, regular payments from a government source, worker's compensation, child support payments made to a household member by an individual legally obligated to make them, or a type the Secretary determines by regulation to be essential to equitable determinations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(d)(18) the income is excluded at the option of the State agency` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the income is wages or salaries, benefits under title I, II, IV, X, XIV, or XVI of the Social Security Act, regular payments from a government source, worker's compensation, child support payments made to a household member by an individual legally obligated to make them, or a type the Secretary determines by regulation to be essential to equitable determinations`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "this paragraph does not authorize a State agency to exclude wages or salaries, benefits under title I, II, IV, X, XIV, or XVI"
        IF `the State agency has chosen to exclude such types of income` AND `the State agency does not consider the income when determining eligibility for cash assistance under part A of title IV, the amount of such assistance, or medical assistance under section 1931`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "at the option of the State agency, any types of income that the State agency does not consider"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (18) reaches only what the State agency has chosen to exclude and does not consider for those programs

-- src:248 | (19) any additional payment under chapter 5 of title 37, or otherwise designated by the Secretary to be appropriate for exclusion under this paragraph, that is received by or from a member of the United States Armed Forces deployed to a designated combat zone, if the additional pay—
-- src:249 | (A) is the result of deployment to or service in a combat zone; and
-- src:250 | (B) was not received immediately prior to serving in a combat zone.
@ref s 2014(d)(19) (src:248-250)
GIVEN `the payment is an additional payment under chapter 5 of title 37, or otherwise designated by the Secretary to be appropriate for exclusion under this paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is received by or from a member of the United States Armed Forces deployed to a designated combat zone` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the result of deployment to or service in a combat zone` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was received immediately prior to serving in a combat zone` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(d)(19) the combat pay is excluded` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF  NOT (`the payment is an additional payment under chapter 5 of title 37, or otherwise designated by the Secretary to be appropriate for exclusion under this paragraph`
                 AND `it is received by or from a member of the United States Armed Forces deployed to a designated combat zone`)
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (19) reaches "any additional payment under chapter 5 of title 37, or otherwise designated by the Secretary to be appropriate for exclusion under this paragraph, that is received by or from a member of the United States Armed Forces deployed to a designated combat zone"
        IF  `it is the result of deployment to or service in a combat zone`
            AND (NOT `it was received immediately prior to serving in a combat zone`)
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "any additional payment under chapter 5 of title 37 ... if the additional pay— (A) is the result of deployment to or service in a combat zone; and (B) was not received immediately prior to serving in a combat zone"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the additional pay— (A) is the result of deployment to or service in a combat zone; and (B) was not received immediately prior to serving in a combat zone" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a))

-- COUNTING WHAT IS LEFT. The paragraphs above say which items are excluded; these say how much of an item is counted.
-- The $30 and $300 limits of paragraphs (2) and (8) are quarterly, and an item is received monthly: the Act does not say how a quarterly limit
-- is shared among the months (finding F-D1). Assumed, not ruled: the share of the quarter's amount that the limit excludes applies to each month's amount alike.
GIVEN `the monthly amount of the item, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of it received in the quarter, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the dollars excluded in the quarter, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2014(d) the monthly dollars excluded under a quarterly limit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the amount of it received in the quarter, in dollars` AT MOST 0 THEN 0
        OTHERWISE `the monthly amount of the item, in dollars` TIMES (`the dollars excluded in the quarter, in dollars` DIVIDED BY `the amount of it received in the quarter, in dollars`)

-- src:224 | Household income for purposes of the supplemental nutrition assistance program shall include all income from whatever source excluding only—
@ref s 2014(d), the chapeau (src:224)
GIVEN `the monthly amount of the item, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `a paragraph of subsection (d) excludes the item in full` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dollars of the item excluded in part each month, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2014(d) the monthly amount of the item that counts as income` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a paragraph of subsection (d) excludes the item in full` THEN 0
        IF `the dollars of the item excluded in part each month, in dollars` GREATER THAN `the monthly amount of the item, in dollars` THEN 0
        OTHERWISE `the monthly amount of the item, in dollars` MINUS `the dollars of the item excluded in part each month, in dollars`

-- src:224 | Household income for purposes of the supplemental nutrition assistance program shall include all income from whatever source excluding only—
@ref s 2014(d), the chapeau (src:224)
GIVEN `the monthly amounts of the items that count as income` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `the reduction under paragraph (9) of the other income that is included` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2014(d) household income` MEANS
    sum `the monthly amounts of the items that count as income` MINUS `the reduction under paragraph (9) of the other income that is included`
